      "problem": "Find $|z|$ if $z=2c-5d\\text{i},$ where $c$ and $d$ are real numbers.",
      "worked_solution": "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=2c-5d\\text{i},$ we have $a=2c$ and $b=-5d.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|2c-5d\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{(2c)^{2}+(-5d)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{c}^{2}+25{d}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
