      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the magnitude of the number $z=\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The imaginary number $\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}$ is equivalent to the complex number $z=0+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}.$\n\nWe know that for a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of $z=0+\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{i}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|z| & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
